@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
@type = "provisioning.integration"

Feature: Koroneiki to Provisioning Employee Integration
	Testing employee sync updates in Provisioning caused by changes in Koroneiki.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I generate static variables for a support user
	* I rename the first support user variables
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue1}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue1}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue1}  |
	| Group         | Employees                       |
	* I generate static variables for a support user
	* I rename the second support user variables
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | ${staticScreenNameValue2}       |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue2}            |
	| First Name    | ${staticContactFirstNameValue2} |
	| Last Name     | ${staticContactLastNameValue2}  |
	| Group         | Employees                       |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	| Updated Partner   |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Platinum Subscription"
	* I synchronize the account entitlement definition with the name "Gold Subscription"
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailValue1} |
	| ${staticEmailValue2} |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta should sync correctly to provisioning.

	Given I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Liferay,"
	And I click on the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	And I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | ${staticEmailValue1} |
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" and the following values
	| Name          | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1} |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue1}                                           |
	| Role          | Member                                                         |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                                                       |
	When I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "${staticScreenNameValue1}"
	Then I should be able to view a user on the provisioning index with the name "${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1}" and the following values
	| Name               | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1}                     |
	| Email Address      | ${staticEmailValue1}                                                               |
	| Entitlements       | Customer, Customer - Commerce, Customer - DXP, Customer - Portal, Liferay Employee |
	| Number of Accounts | 1                                                                                  |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                                                                           |

Scenario: Remove Liferay employee
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	New Liferay employees who are removed from the Liferay Inc org on okta should sync correctly to provisioning.

	Given I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	When I remove the okta user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" from the okta group "Employees"
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" via automatic sync
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Liferay,"
	And I click on the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	And I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | ${staticEmailValue1} |
	Then I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}"
	When I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "${staticScreenNameValue1}"
	Then I should be able to view a user on the provisioning index with the name "${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1}" and the following values
	| Name               | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1} |
	| Email Address      | ${staticEmailValue1}                                           |
	| Entitlements       |                                                                |
	| Number of Accounts | 0                                                              |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                                                       |

Scenario: Deactivate Liferay employee
	New Liferay employees who are deactivated on okta should sync correctly to provisioning.

	Given I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	When I deactivate the user with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" from okta
	Then the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should not be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Liferay,"
	And I click on the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." on the provisioning index
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	And I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | ${staticEmailValue1} |
	Then I should not be able to view the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}"
	When I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "${staticScreenNameValue1}"
	Then I should be able to view a user on the provisioning index with the name "${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1}" and the following values
	| Name               | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1} |
	| Email Address      | ${staticEmailValue1}                                           |
	| Entitlements       |                                                                |
	| Number of Accounts | 0                                                              |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                                                       |

Scenario: View employee added as a Support Requester to a Professional Services Managed Services account
	New Liferay employees who are added to koroneiki via okta whose projects have the Professional Services Managed Services purchase should not be counted on the developer counter

	Given I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" added via automatic sync
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" added via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" via automatic sync
	And the account with the name "Liferay, Inc." should be assigned the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue2}" via automatic sync
	When I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - DXP"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Portal"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Customer - Commerce"
	And I synchronize the contact entitlement definition with the name "Liferay Employee"
	And I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | ${staticEmailValue1}                       |
	| Contact First Name                     | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1}            |
	| Contact Last Name                      | ${staticContactLastNameValue1}             |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | ${staticEmailValue2}                       |
	| Owner First Name                       | ${staticContactFirstNameValue2}            |
	| Owner Last Name                        | ${staticContactLastNameValue2}             |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Professional Services- Managed Services    |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	And I create a team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}"
	And I assign the team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" on the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" to the following roles
	| First Line Support |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	Then I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I should be able to view the following account values in the account details page
	| Name           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Code           | PROKORKORPRO                  |
	| State          | ACTIVE                        |
	| Support Region | United States                 |
	| Country        | United States                 |
	| SLA            | Platinum                      |
	| Support Seats  | 0 / 10 Filled                 |
	| Tier           | T4                            |
	| FLS Partner    | Koroneiki Partner             |
	And I click on the "Contacts" tab
	And I search and filter the accounts details page using the following parameters
	| Keyword | ${staticEmailValue1} |
	Then I should be able to view the contact with the email address "${staticEmailValue1}" and the following values
	| Name          | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1} |
	| Email Address | ${staticEmailValue1}                                           |
	| Role          | Support Requester                                              |
	| Role          | Support Administrator                                          |
	| User Status   | VERIFIED                                                       |
	When I go to the user index page
	And I search the users page using the keyword "${staticScreenNameValue1}"
	Then I should be able to view a user on the provisioning index with the name "${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1}" and the following values
	| Name               | ${staticContactFirstNameValue1} ${staticContactLastNameValue1}                     |
	| Email Address      | ${staticEmailValue1}                                                               |
	| Entitlements       | Customer, Customer - Commerce, Customer - DXP, Customer - Portal, Liferay Employee |
	| Number of Accounts | 2                                                                                  |
	| Status             | VERIFIED                                                                           |
	Then I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Professional Services - Managed Services" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |
	And I should be able to view a product purchase on koroneiki made by the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" for the product "Platinum Subscription" with the following values
	| Quantity | 1        | |
	| Status   | Approved | |